$ ramplus profile plan zswap-zstd --set zswap.compressor=842
Plan: profile zswap-zstd — modified by the user
Command: ramplus profile apply zswap-zstd --set zswap.compressor=842
Profile: zswap + zstd. zswap on: zstd, zsmalloc, pool up to 20% of RAM; sysctl as in default.
Evidence: none (no scripts/bench.sh results on a real SSD)

Parameters
  PARAMETER         NOW      NEW          CURRENT SOURCE
  zswap.enabled     N     →  Y            cmdline (zswap.enabled=1)
  zswap.compressor  lzo   →  842 (--set)  kernel default
  zswap.zpool       zbud  →  zsmalloc     kernel default
  unchanged: zswap.max_pool_percent=20, vm.swappiness=60, vm.page-cluster=3, vm.watermark_scale_factor=10, vm.vfs_cache_pressure=100

sysctl order at boot: /usr/lib/sysctl.d/30-tune.conf (vm.page-cluster=0) → 99-ramplus.conf → /etc/sysctl.d/99-sysctl.conf (vm.swappiness=10)

Checks
  [ok]   root: running as root
  [warn] status: experimental profile: not confirmed by scripts/bench.sh on a real SSD — applied only with explicit confirmation (in scripts: --experimental)
  [info] --set: profile modified by the user: zswap.compressor=842 (in the profile: zstd)
  [FAIL] compressor: 842 is not available in the kernel: not in /proc/crypto and no crypto/842.ko module — choose another one (--set zswap.compressor=...)
  [FAIL] zram: a zram generator is installed (/etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf): zswap on top of zram is pointless (compressed pages get compressed again). Disable zram or add --force
  [warn] cmdline: /proc/cmdline sets zswap.enabled=1: the kernel applies it at boot, then ramplus-zswap.service overwrites the profile values — the profile wins. RamPlus does not change the kernel command line or GRUB; to avoid confusion, remove zswap.* from GRUB by hand
  [warn] sysctl: /etc/sysctl.d/99-sysctl.conf sets vm.swappiness=10 and is applied after 99-ramplus.conf — at boot it will override the profile value (60). Remove the key from that file
  [info] original values: first profile apply: the current system values are saved to /var/lib/ramplus/state.json for ramplus profile reset

Steps
   1. zswap.compressor = 842 (write to /sys/module/zswap/parameters/compressor)
   2. zswap.zpool = zsmalloc (write to /sys/module/zswap/parameters/zpool)
   3. zswap.enabled = Y (write to /sys/module/zswap/parameters/enabled)
   4. write /etc/sysctl.d/99-ramplus.conf
   5. write /etc/systemd/system/ramplus-zswap.service
   6. systemctl daemon-reload
   7. systemctl enable ramplus-zswap.service
  (content of files to be written: --verbose)

